te_pool_share":0.5270919878489015,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":100.0,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":0.044512521236149905,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.007698568487576004,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":87.2,"_gate_insider_own":0.08197,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":54.6,"_gate_insider_buying":0.75,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":75.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Third Coast Bancshares, Inc. operates as the bank holding company for Third Coast Bank that provides various commercial banking solutions to small and medium-sized businesses and professionals in Texas, the United States. The company's deposit products include checking, money market, savings, and individual retirement accounts, as well as certificates of deposit. Its loan portfolio consists of commercial and residential real estate loans; construction, development and other loans; commercial and industrial loans; and farmland, consumer, and agricultural loans, as well as lease financing and bond anticipation notes, as well as financial products and services. The company also provides retail and commercial online banking platforms, mobile banking apps, treasury management solutions, merchant card services, and customer digital solutions, as well as debit and credit cards. In addition, it offers state and municipal and mortgage-backed securities, agency collateralized mortgage obligations, the U.S. treasury bonds, and corporate bonds. The company was founded in 2008 and is headquartered in Humble, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Bart O. Caraway CPA | Founder, Chairman, President & CEO | Age 54 | Compensation: $2.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 482 people. Revenue per employee of $433K ranks in the below the sector median among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 22%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $100K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Third Coast Bancshares, Inc. is a small-cap financial services business with a $632M market cap on $209M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +19% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +6.1pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 38% against a 8% cost of capital \u2014 a 30-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $48M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 23 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, with adequate 0.77\u00d7 cash conversion.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 0.5\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 8.2% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 11% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 50% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Insiders are net buyers (75% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Financial Services peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Third Coast Bancshares Appoints Liz Eber as Executive VP and Chief Legal & Operating Officer","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/third-coast-bancshares-appoints-liz-eber-as-executive-vp-and-chief-legal-operating-officer","date":"2026-11-24","timestamp":1795557470.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.128,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":["leadership"]},{"title":"Third Coast Bancshares Submits S-4 Registration for Acquisition of Great Plains Bancshares","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/third-coast-bancshares-submits-s-4-registrat